{{!-- Forced-SSO hand-off. This page exists instead of an HTTP redirect because Chrome checks a
form submission's redirect target against the SUBMITTING page's form-action: when a session expires
mid-form, the browser follows POST /admin/x -> /admin/login -> the provider as one submission, and
the admin policy's `form-action 'self'` kills that last hop, so the form silently does nothing. A
navigation this page starts is not part of that submission, so the policy no longer applies to it.

The per-route relaxation that lets the account page's Re-authenticate button redirect to a provider
(OAUTH_REDIRECT_FORM_DIRECTIVES) cannot help here: the policy being enforced belongs to whichever
admin page held the form, which is any of them.

location.replace() rather than a meta refresh: it leaves no history entry, so Back does not land
here and bounce the user straight out again, which is how the HTTP redirect behaved. The link is
what a browser that did not run the script gets.

The navigation itself is started from views/layout/login.hbs, above the stylesheets: an inline
script here in the body cannot run until those have loaded, which is long enough for this card to
paint and read as a flash of the login page. What stays here is the markup a browser without
JavaScript needs. --}}
<h1 class="text-base-content mb-2 text-xl font-semibold">Signing in&mldr;</h1>

<p class="text-base-content/60 mb-6 text-sm">Taking you to {{providers.oidc.name}} to sign in.</p>

{{> ui/btn label="Continue" href=ssoRedirectUrl id="sso-continue" icon="icon-[tabler--login-2]" class="btn-block"}}
